Cause/correction: the script compared the byte result of
obcppackets.receivepacket() to a Python text string (`'OK'`). The N7 module
returns bytes, so that assertion stopped later script operations; the upstream
execute API still returned true, confirming that its Boolean is not a reliable
interpreter-success oracle. The integration test was corrected to compare with
`b'OK'`, and to assert callback effects after execution. The focused test then
passed. This is test-oracle correction evidence, not an N7 engine qualification.
